claim.claim-text:
37. A method for bit stuffing handling in a HDLC system, comprising the steps of: adding of an extra character in sequences in original information bits to be transmitted, which resembles any flag pattern, adding a start/stop flag in front of and after the bits to be transmitted, defin- ing a frame to be transmitted; transmitting said frame; receiving transmitted frames of information bits; 

 first searching said transmitted information bits for a first start/stop flag bit pattern; and when said first start/stop flag bit pattern has been detected, cancelling an extra character in sequences in said transmitted information bits which resembles any flag pattern, searching said transmitted information bits for a second start/stop flag bit pattern or abort flag bit pattern, until said second start/stop flag bit pattern or abort flag bit pattern is detected, c h a r a c t e r i z e d b y prior to the step of adding a start/stop flag, the steps of: creating a first queue (A) of said original bits; selecting the n first bits from said first queue (A), creating a first bit sequence of n bits; comparing said first bit sequence with prestored transmission bit stuffing data, comprising, for each possible combination of bit values in said first bit se- quence, transmission shift data (TNS) and transmission sequence data; adding data derived from said transmission sequence data corresponding to said first bit sequence to a second queue (B); removing a number of bits from said first queue (A) equal to the transmission shift data (TNS) corresponding to said first bit sequence; and repeating said selecting, comparing, adding and removing steps until said first queue (A) is empty; and in that said first searching step in turn comprises the steps of: selecting the m first bits from a third queue (C) of bits, consisting of said transmitted information bits, creating a second bit sequence of m bits; comparing said second bit sequence with prestored reception bit stuffing data, comprising, for each possible combination of bit values in said second bit sequence, reception shift data (RNS), reception sequence data, start/stop flag indicator (OF) and abort flag indicator (AF); removing a number of bits from said third queue (C) equal to the reception shift data (NS) corresponding to said second bit sequence; and 

 repeating said selecting, comparing and removing steps of said first searching step until said second bit sequence corresponds to a set start/stop flag indicator (OF); and in that said cancelling step in turn comprises the steps of: selecting the m first bits from said third queue (C) of bits, creating a third bit sequence of m bits; comparing said third bit sequence with said prestored reception bit stuffing data; when said third bit sequence corresponds to a non-set value of both said start/stop flag indicator (OF) and said abort flag indicator (AF), adding data derived from the reception sequence data corresponding to said third bit sequence to a fourth queue (D), and removing a number of bits from said third queue (C) equal to the reception shift data (RNS) corresponding to said third bit sequence; when said third bit sequence corresponds to a non-set value of both said start/stop flag indicator (OF) and said abort flag indicator (AF), repeating said selecting, comparing, adding and removing steps of said cancelling step until said third bit sequence corresponds to a set start/stop flag indicator (OF) or a set abort flag indicator (AF); and by the step of: repeating first searching and cancelling steps until said third queue (C) is empty.
